Azure File Provenance Workbook
The implementation will use a Microsoft Sentinel / Azure Monitor Workbook to investigate a file using its full path or SharePoint URL.

The workbook will contain:
View	Function
File search	Enter a full file path or SharePoint URL
Activity timeline	Show recorded creation, access, modification, download, rename and movement events
Movement graph	Connect observed source and destination locations
User activity	Identify accounts associated with file events
Evidence table	Show timestamps, event types, file identifiers, hashes and audit references
The initial version will query OfficeActivity and DeviceFileEvents in the selected Log Analytics workspace.

Azure Workbooks supports native node-and-edge graph visualisations, so a separate graph database is not required for this initial implementation. 

Scope: This is an evidence-based investigation workbook, not a complete file-lineage engine. It will show recorded movements and the latest observed location, without treating an unverified destination or a matching filename as proof that two files are identical.
